  "chapter": {
    "number": 49,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(50) A Psalm",
          {
            "noteId": 92
          },
          "for Asaph."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The God of gods, the Lord, has spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun to the going down thereof.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Out of Sion comes the excellence of his beauty.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God, our God, shall come manifestly, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall be kindled before him, and round about him there shall be a very great tempest.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall summon the heaven above, and the earth, that he may judge his people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Assemble you⌃ his saints to him, those that have engaged in a covenant with him upon sacrifices.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the heavens shall declare his righteousness: for God is judge. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear, my people, and I will speak to you, O Israel: and I will testify to you: I am God, your God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will not reprove you on account of your sacrifices; for your whole burnt offerings are before me continually.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will take no bullocks out of your house, nor he-goats out of your flocks.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For all the wild beasts of the thicket are mine, the cattle on the mountains, and oxen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I know all the birds of the sky; and the beauty of the field is mine.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I should be hungry, I will not tell you: for the world is mine, and the fullness of it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Offer to God the sacrifice of praise; and pay your vows to the Most High.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And call upon me in the day of affliction; and I will deliver you, and you shall glorify me. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But to the sinner God has said, Why do you declare my ordinances, and take up my covenant in your mouth?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Whereas you have hated instruction, and have cast my words behind you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If you saw a thief, you",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 93
          },
          {
            "text": "ran along with him, and have cast in your lot with adulterers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your mouth has multiplied wickedness, and your tongue has framed deceit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 94
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did sit and speak against your brother, and did scandalize your mother's son.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "These things you did, and I kept silence: you thought wickedly that I should be like you, but I will reprove you, and set your offenses before you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Now consider these things, you⌃ that forget God, lest he rend you, and there is no deliverer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sacrifice of praise will glorify me: and",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 95
          },
          {
            "text": "that is the way wherein I will show to him the salvation of God.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
